id: pm-gh1647
title: "GH-1647: acquireLock / acquireLockLease follow a symlinked locks directory and create the lock outside the tracker"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1647 (found by pm-rl's state-confinement guarantee, unbraind/pm-rl#107): when the tracker's locks directory (or a lock entry's parent) is a symlink, acquireLock and acquireLockLease follow it and create the lock outside the tracker, so two writers resolving the path differently share no exclusion point and an extension cannot close the check/use window with its own pathname check. The SDK must refuse a symlinked or swapped lock directory with a typed lock_path_unsafe error and never create a lock outside the tracker."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: bug,concurrency,"gh:1647",locks,sdk,security
created_at: "2026-11-01T10:48:40.483Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T19:14:39.750Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:25.492Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:25.492Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "acquireLock and acquireLockLease refuse with code lock_path_unsafe when the tracker's locks directory or any component between the tracker root and the lock entry is a symlink or not a directory, or the lock entry itself is a symlink, and no file is created outside the tracker; A swap of the locks directory between the confinement check and lock creation is detected by comparing the created lock's identity with the confined directory entry, and the acquisition refuses with lock_path_unsafe (lock_directory_replaced) without ever deleting outside the tracker, leaving the stray lock in place and saying so in context.required; Regression tests cover a pre-existing symlinked locks directory and a swap during acquisition for both acquireLock and acquireLockLease, and the refusal is documented in docs/SDK.md"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "New core/lock/lock-confinement.ts: lstat-walk of every component between tracker root and lock parent before mkdir or the cleanup gate (refuses lock_directory_symlink, lock_directory_not_directory, lock_path_outside_tracker); a symlinked lock entry refuses lock_entry_symlink; after open(wx) the handle dev/ino must equal lstat(lockPath) inside the same directory identity, else lock_directory_replaced. The refusal never unlinks lockPath and never deletes outside the tracker: the stray lock stays where the swap pointed and context.required says so per reason. pm gc --scope locks refuses a symlinked locks dir. Mid-operation swaps after the one-time check are tracked in pm-jd2zim. Documented in docs/SDK.md."
expected_result: acquireLock and acquireLockLease never create a lock outside the tracker; symlinked or swapped lock directories refuse with a typed lock_path_unsafe error.
actual_result: "Confinement specs pass for a pre-existing symlink (both entrypoints), a regular-file locks entry (all platforms), a symlinked entry with per-reason recovery text, a swap during acquisition leaving the stray lock outside untouched, a swap-back that preserves a peer lock, a symlinked tracker root, and the gc refusal. Lock unit tests, the full suite and 100% coverage pass."
